907
00:44:24,643 --> 00:44:25,223
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, I don't know.

908
00:44:25,243 --> 00:44:26,785
[SPEAKER_03]: Probably not more than two and a half hours or so.

909
00:44:26,825 --> 00:44:28,346
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't know, I don't know.

910
00:44:28,726 --> 00:44:30,488
[SPEAKER_03]: It'd take five hours to play that today.

911
00:44:38,550 --> 00:44:42,811
[SPEAKER_03]: Who was, there must have been some hitter which gave you some trouble though, wasn't there anybody?

912
00:44:45,272 --> 00:44:49,714
[SPEAKER_02]: You take these hitters at show clubs, they give them more trouble than anybody.

913
00:44:51,495 --> 00:44:56,957
[SPEAKER_02]: They're standing right on that plate, and you have to get that ball over there.

914
00:44:56,977 --> 00:44:59,898
[SPEAKER_02]: Now you take Ruth, and then he stood a little farther away.

915
00:44:59,918 --> 00:45:00,919
[SPEAKER_02]: Now you take Cobb.

916
00:45:01,999 --> 00:45:03,500
[SPEAKER_02]: I never had any trouble with Cobb.

917
00:45:04,140 --> 00:45:04,900
[SPEAKER_03]: How'd you pitch him?

918
00:45:05,421 --> 00:45:06,141
[SPEAKER_02]: Fast ball.

919
00:45:08,868 --> 00:45:09,829
[SPEAKER_02]: Would it be inside?

920
00:45:10,569 --> 00:45:13,910
[SPEAKER_02]: Because Cobb is a fella, he hit left field all the time.

921
00:45:13,950 --> 00:45:16,351
[SPEAKER_02]: The longest field where he could be any mile, he was fast.

922
00:45:16,732 --> 00:45:18,132
[SPEAKER_02]: He'd bury someone and pull the ball.

923
00:45:19,233 --> 00:45:22,634
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, he couldn't push this inside ball that side.

924
00:45:23,174 --> 00:45:24,095
[SPEAKER_02]: And he didn't go by.

925
00:45:24,175 --> 00:45:26,936
[SPEAKER_02]: I'd strike him once or twice every time I'd be in there.

926
00:45:28,576 --> 00:45:31,738
[SPEAKER_02]: And Ruth, all the time, they kept it outside and kept it down low.

927
00:45:31,758 --> 00:45:34,919
[SPEAKER_02]: They couldn't get a hold of it.

928
00:45:40,014 --> 00:45:41,297
[SPEAKER_03]: How about Joe Jackson?

929
00:45:41,978 --> 00:45:44,302
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, he left here while I got over there.

930
00:45:45,665 --> 00:45:46,627
[SPEAKER_02]: He left even then.

931
00:45:46,647 --> 00:45:47,849
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, but you pitched against him.

932
00:45:47,869 --> 00:45:48,290
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, I pitched.

933
00:45:48,471 --> 00:45:49,673
[SPEAKER_03]: How was he to pitch against him?

934
00:46:14,510 --> 00:46:18,172
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, I never associated too much with other players.

935
00:46:18,392 --> 00:46:20,534
[SPEAKER_02]: I was always by myself.

936
00:46:20,594 --> 00:46:21,914
[SPEAKER_03]: Didn't this bother your pitching?

937
00:46:22,835 --> 00:46:25,557
[SPEAKER_03]: Your drinking, or you didn't mix them, huh?

938
00:46:26,658 --> 00:46:29,059
[SPEAKER_02]: I didn't mix them.

939
00:46:29,840 --> 00:46:31,341
[SPEAKER_02]: I got drunk.

940
00:46:31,781 --> 00:46:39,606
[SPEAKER_02]: One time, my brother came over, a craven, him and another fellow, and they were there two days and I didn't pitch.

941
00:46:43,710 --> 00:46:47,671
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, well, I'll probably pitch tomorrow.

942
00:46:47,691 --> 00:46:49,211
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, I'll take us out.

943
00:46:50,871 --> 00:46:52,012
[SPEAKER_02]: So I pitched tomorrow.

944
00:46:52,672 --> 00:46:54,232
[SPEAKER_02]: The next day, I took them out.

945
00:46:54,312 --> 00:46:57,833
[SPEAKER_02]: I took them across the river in Cleveland, across that river bridge there.

946
00:46:58,333 --> 00:47:00,093
[SPEAKER_02]: Some police district down there.

947
00:47:00,113 --> 00:47:01,233
[SPEAKER_02]: What's 25th Street?

948
00:47:01,353 --> 00:47:02,514
[SPEAKER_02]: Moonshine, right there.

949
00:47:03,154 --> 00:47:05,134
[SPEAKER_02]: Listen, I was a drunk.

950
00:47:05,974 --> 00:47:08,395
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know why I'd be able to come to Euclid Alabama.

951
00:47:08,455 --> 00:47:10,695
[SPEAKER_02]: I'd better knock down two or three safety zones.

952
00:47:11,682 --> 00:47:12,802
[SPEAKER_02]: And nobody stopped me.

953
00:47:13,002 --> 00:47:17,623
[SPEAKER_02]: I went in the hotel near the garage on the bottom.

954
00:47:18,483 --> 00:47:21,424
[SPEAKER_02]: I go in there, and I had to take my car to the second story.

955
00:47:21,644 --> 00:47:25,905
[SPEAKER_02]: I took it up there, and when I came out, I told my brother, and I said, walk straight through.

956
00:47:26,025 --> 00:47:28,285
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, somebody might see us.

957
00:47:28,346 --> 00:47:30,086
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm drunker than anyone.

958
00:47:30,706 --> 00:47:32,806
[SPEAKER_02]: So I go up in the room.

959
00:47:32,986 --> 00:47:33,887
[SPEAKER_02]: I go up in the room.

960
00:47:37,908 --> 00:47:40,108
[SPEAKER_02]: The next morning, I get up good and early,

961
00:47:40,808 --> 00:47:44,031
[SPEAKER_02]: I got on the phone, I called the ball club up.

962
00:47:44,471 --> 00:47:45,912
[SPEAKER_02]: No one was out there.

963
00:47:46,653 --> 00:47:48,655
[SPEAKER_02]: And I told them this is exactly what happened.

964
00:47:49,655 --> 00:47:50,656
[SPEAKER_02]: I told them everything.

965
00:47:52,438 --> 00:47:58,463
[SPEAKER_02]: So when I went out and the speaker came in, the whole meeting in the morning, he said, there were phone calls up there.

966
00:47:58,523 --> 00:48:00,284
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, the hell with it.

967
00:48:02,226 --> 00:48:03,447
[SPEAKER_02]: But I took care of myself.

968
00:48:03,467 --> 00:48:05,609
[SPEAKER_02]: I didn't want to go out and have a couple of drinks today.

969
00:48:06,049 --> 00:48:07,050
[SPEAKER_02]: It didn't bother me any.

970
00:48:08,359 --> 00:48:09,119
[SPEAKER_03]: You look pretty good.

971
00:48:09,240 --> 00:48:17,785
[SPEAKER_02]: But I never drunk before a ball game, you know what I mean.

972
00:48:18,926 --> 00:48:22,088
[SPEAKER_03]: As long as you were all ready to go and you were pitching.

973
00:48:22,168 --> 00:48:24,609
[SPEAKER_02]: I was ready to pitch any time of the day.

974
00:48:24,689 --> 00:48:27,491
[SPEAKER_02]: Many a time I had a notion to go from the bench right out of the box.

975
00:48:28,232 --> 00:48:29,913
